scientists have probed the universe for  signs of life beyond Earth for years and  now recent discoveries strongly suggest  that alien life could in fact exist  earlier this year NASA made a  groundbreaking announcement that liquid  water exists on Mars today in fact  scientists estimate that at least one  fifth of Mars was covered in oceans  about four-and-a-half billion years ago  this means that both fossilized and  living organisms could be on the planet  but water isn't exclusive to Mars  scientists have confirmed a massive  global ocean on Saturn's moon Enceladus  beneath it's icy outer shell and  chemicals found in the water suggest  that this ocean floor is lined with  hydrothermal vents the same vents that  may have spawned life on Earth and  Jupiter's moon Europa could Harbor more  water than Earth itself brownish veins  on the surface point to seeping liquid  water from the moon's mantle and both  America and Europe have invested  hundreds of millions of dollars in space  missions to explore this further  Saturn's largest moon Titan is the only  other body in our solar system with  lakes on the surface but these lakes are  made of liquid methane not water and  while water is essential to the  formation of life as we know it  scientists have shown how methane based  oxygen free living cells might exist on  Titan in addition to water Comet and  asteroid impacts are considered key to  the formation of life impacts cause  amino acids to combine and form the  building blocks of life and there could  be comets in other planetary systems  that are doing this right now in fact  the Milky Way may not be the most  hospitable galaxy for life according to  a scientific study other galaxies could  host 10,000 times more habitable planets  than the Milky Way one planet that  scientists have discovered in our own  galaxy is being dubbed  earth 2.0 kepler 452b  an earth-like planet 1,400 light-years  away  and its size orbit Sun and age provide  the opportunity for life to arise  somewhere on the surface should all the  necessary ingredients and conditions for  life on the planet exist according to  NASA's John Jenkins and kepler 452b  is not the only place scientists are  looking for life they are using the  Allen telescope array to determine if an  alien civilization lives in an unusual  star system 1,500 light-years away  though chances are very low large hunks  of matter orbiting star could be part of  an alien built mega structure known as a  Dyson swarm with so many scientific  discoveries that point to  extraterrestrial life many believe the  question shouldn't be is there life  beyond Earth but rather will we ever  find it
 

